{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>With the fat on the breast</b> — what appears from this verse according to the plain sense is that the breast is waved together with the fats, and not the thigh. And the verse that says (Leviticus 9:21), \"And the breasts and the right thigh Aaron waved as a wave offering\" — this means that afterwards he would go back and wave them by themselves. But our Sages said (Menahot 62a) that he would place the fats on the hands of the owners, with the breast and thigh above them. And according to their view, the verse mentioned waving with regard to the breast alone in order to derive what they said (Torat Kohanim, chapter 16:2): if they became impure and one of them remained, from where do we learn that it requires waving? The verse says, \"the breast, to wave it\"."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:28.738632839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}